**How to implement.** Every place that builds a `MaterialEntry` from engine properties states its physics as `MaterialComplexity` data first, while `properties` is still a field (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`). The script comparisons then prove that no number moves before step 13 changes the record (.spec-md §3.2). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`: `material` (`:85-88`) takes a `MaterialComplexity` and saves `properties = complexity.toProperties` with the complexity. Each caller passes the script's material as data, and the script side keeps the script's own properties. `constantN 1.78052` (`:273`) becomes `EpsWithoutDispValue (IsotropicTransparent (RefractionIndex 1.78052))`. `dispersiveGlass` (`:357`; the script's n² = 1 + Σ bᵢλ²/(λ² − cᵢ) in µm, `:344-353`) becomes one isotropic dispersive segment over 300–700 nm whose axis is the Domain Sellmeier lowering `(Sellmeier { b = [ 1.43; 0.65 ]; c = [ 0.073 * 0.073; 0.12 * 0.12 ]; wavelengthUnit = Micrometer; thermoOptic = None }).toEpsAxis` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:DispersionModel.toEpsAxis`). `langasiteOpticalProperties` (`:386`) becomes one uniaxial dispersive segment over 250–600 nm with `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteOrdinaryIndexLaw` and `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteExtraordinaryIndexLaw`, and `active = Some (PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw)` (step 10). `siliconOpticalProperties` (`:387`) becomes one isotropic dispersive segment over 250–600 nm with `PublishedLawAxis SiliconIndexLaw`. The glasses and the vacuum spacer (`:410-411`, `:442-443`) become `IsotropicTransparent` of `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass`, `RefractionIndex.vacuum`, `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass175` and `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass150`. For the EUV layers, `euvStack`, `euvAgainstIncidence` and `euvAgainstWaveLength` (`:477-509`) take each layer as a `ComplexRefractionIndex`. The table stores `IsotropicAbsorbing` of it, and the script's system builds it as the scripts do: `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex`, then `OpticalProperties.fromEpsion` (`Berreman/OpticalProperties/Standard.fs:91`, `:110`). The EUV.fsx facts pass 1 − δ + iβ from `Eps.euvMolybdenumDelta` / `Eps.euvMolybdenumBeta` and `Eps.euvSiliconDelta` / `Eps.euvSiliconBeta`, and the EUV__002 facts pass their own (0.100, 0.045) and (0.006, 0.002); `euvComplex` (`:492-494`) is deleted. Every magnetic aspect is `None`, and so is every active aspect except Langasite's. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `a minted MaterialId round-trips create-store-lookup through the library` (`:141-160`): the entry carries a constant `IsotropicTransparent (RefractionIndex 1.5)` complexity with `properties = complexity.toProperties`. The lookup assertion compares the resolved `getEps` at 400, 600 and 800 nm with the complexity's own, through the file's `epsClose 1e-12` (`:28`), not by reference, because step 13 derives `properties` on every read. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs`: `vacuumProperties` (`:46-56`) becomes `vacuumPlaceholderComplexity : MaterialComplexity` = `{ eps = EpsWithoutDispValue (IsotropicAbsorbing (ComplexRefractionIndex (Complex.create 1.0 0.0))); magnetic = None; active = None }`. Its composition is the same `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of 1 + 0i under the vacuum μ and ρ. `dtoToEntry` (`:93-111`) sets `properties` from it and carries it as the complexity, and the 'view-only until the §D.9 mapping lands' comment (`:106-107`) is deleted. Such an entry is now vacuum term data, editable like any constant material. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs` gains `a metadata-only library file re-imports each entry as vacuum data`. It exports the described `builtInEntries` (filtered as `:96-98` filters them) to a file under the test run's output directory and re-imports it; every imported entry's `complexity` MUST equal the vacuum value of (3).

**Acceptance.** After every fixture states its physics as data, ui-tests (FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass, with every script comparison within its 1e-6 tolerance; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with the new ExportImportTests fact and the reworked minted-id fact; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.
